EOF

chmod +x analyze-cluster-logs.sh
./analyze-cluster-logs.sh cluster1
Expected output: a conditions: block showing ManagedClusterConditionAvailable: True, zero or more matched error lines, a listing of bootstrap/hub-kubeconfig secrets, and a human-readable availability message such as "Managed cluster is available".

Step 2: Collect basic health metrics via the CLI (no external Prometheus dependency required)

cat > collect-metrics.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

echo "=== RHACM Metrics Collection ==="

PROMETHEUS_ROUTE=$(oc get route -n open-cluster-management-observability prometheus -o jsonpath='{.spec.host}' 2>/dev/null)

if [ -n "$PROMETHEUS_ROUTE" ]; then
    echo "Prometheus endpoint: https://$PROMETHEUS_ROUTE"
    TOKEN=$(oc whoami -t)

    echo "=== Cluster Health Metrics ==="
    curl -sk -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
        "https://$PROMETHEUS_ROUTE/api/v1/query?query=cluster:cpu_usage_cores:sum" | jq .

    echo "=== Managed Cluster Info Metric ==="
    curl -sk -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
        "https://$PROMETHEUS_ROUTE/api/v1/query?query=acm_managed_cluster_info" | jq .
else
    echo "Observability stack not available, falling back to basic cluster status..."
    oc get managedclusters -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,STATUS:.status.conditions[0].type,AVAILABLE:.status.conditions[0].status
fi
EOF

chmod +x collect-metrics.sh
./collect-metrics.sh
Deliverable: either a JSON-formatted Prometheus query response (if observability is enabled), or a table listing each managed cluster's name, condition type, and availability status. Confirm both cluster1 and cluster2 appear with AVAILABLE: True.

