Task 3: Troubleshooting Deployment Failures and Policy Violations
Subtask 3.1: Diagnosing and Fixing a Broken Application Deployment
Step 1: Create the application deployment troubleshooter script

cat > app-deployment-troubleshooter.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

APP_NAME=${1:-"sample-app"}
NAMESPACE=${2:-"default"}

echo "=== Application Deployment Troubleshooter ==="
echo "Application: $APP_NAME"
echo "Namespace: $NAMESPACE"

echo "=== Application Status ==="
oc get application "$APP_NAME" -n "$NAMESPACE" -o yaml 2>/dev/null || echo "Application not found"

echo "=== Subscription Status ==="
SUBSCRIPTIONS=$(oc get subscription -n "$NAMESPACE" -l app="$APP_NAME" --no-headers 2>/dev/null)
if [ -n "$SUBSCRIPTIONS" ]; then
    oc get subscription -n "$NAMESPACE" -l app="$APP_NAME" -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,PHASE:.status.phase,MESSAGE:.status.message
else
    echo "No subscriptions found for application $APP_NAME"
fi

echo "=== Placement Rules ==="
oc get placementrule -n "$NAMESPACE" -l app="$APP_NAME" -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,SATISFIED:.status.satisfied 2>/dev/null

echo "=== Placement Decisions ==="
oc get placementdecision -n "$NAMESPACE" -l app="$APP_NAME" 2>/dev/null

echo "=== Deployed Resources on Target Clusters ==="
for cluster in $(oc get managedclusters -o name | cut -d'/' -f2); do
    echo "Checking cluster: $cluster"
    oc get manifestwork -n "$cluster" 2>/dev/null | grep "$APP_NAME" || echo "No manifestwork found on $cluster"
done

echo "=== Common Issues Check ==="
echo "1. Image pull / mount errors:"
oc get events -n "$NAMESPACE" --field-selector reason=Failed 2>/dev/null | grep -i "image\|pull" || echo "None found"

echo "2. Scheduling failures:"
oc get events -n "$NAMESPACE" --field-selector reason=FailedScheduling 2>/dev/null || echo "None found"

echo "3. RBAC issues:"
oc get events -n "$NAMESPACE" --field-selector reason=FailedCreate 2>/dev/null | grep -i "forbidden\|unauthorized" || echo "None found"
EOF

chmod +x app-deployment-troubleshooter.sh
Step 2: Deploy a sample application with an intentional placement misconfiguration, then run the troubleshooter against it

cat > problematic-app.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: app.k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: problematic-app
  namespace: default
spec:
  componentKinds:
  - group: apps.open-cluster-management.io
    kind: Subscription
  descriptor: {}
  selector:
    matchExpressions:
    - key: app
      operator: In
      values:
      - problematic-app
---
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Subscription
metadata:
  name: problematic-app-subscription
  namespace: default
  labels:
    app: problematic-app
spec:
  channel: default/sample-channel
  placement:
    placementRef:
      name: problematic-app-placement
      kind: PlacementRule
---
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementRule
metadata:
  name: problematic-app-placement
  namespace: default
  labels:
    app: problematic-app
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    matchLabels:
      environment: nonexistent  # No managed cluster has this label - causes placement failure
EOF

oc apply -f problematic-app.yaml

echo "Testing troubleshooter..."
./app-deployment-troubleshooter.sh problematic-app default
Expected output: the Application and Subscription resources are found, but the PlacementRule shows SATISFIED: False (or no PlacementDecision is created at all), and the "Deployed Resources on Target Clusters" section reports "No manifestwork found" on both cluster1 and cluster2 â�� confirming the application never actually shipped anywhere due to the bad clusterSelector.

Step 3: Fix the placement issue and re-verify

cat > fixed-placement.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementRule
metadata:
  name: problematic-app-placement
  namespace: default
  labels:
    app: problematic-app
spec:
